# .dockerignore — repo root. The Dockerfiles in webui/ are built with the repo
# root as context (docker build -f webui/Dockerfile.* .), so this filters what
# COPY sees. Primarily:
#  - webui/node_modules/: the node build stages run `npm ci` in-image; copying
#    the host's node_modules over it would replace Linux native binaries
#    (@esbuild/*, @rollup/rollup-*) with darwin ones and break the build.
#  - data/: huge, gitignored pipeline data — must never enter images
#    (defense in depth; the public API mounts /data read-only at runtime).
#  - test code / caches: keep internals out of the shipped images.

# --- frontend build dirs (rebuilt in-image) ---
webui/node_modules/
webui/dist/
webui/dist-public/

# --- python caches / environments ---
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# --- test code (internal; not needed in images) ---
webui/api/tests/
webui/api/__tests__/
tests/

# --- repo/VCS and workspace internals ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.superpowers/
.claude/
.cursor/

# --- pipeline data (never bake into images) ---
data/

# --- secrets (defense in depth for local builds; runtime uses env/mounts) ---
praw.ini
.env
.env.*
token.json
credentials.json

# --- tooling/docs not needed at runtime ---
docs/
*.md
!README.md
